ounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays).\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01ECzukfLVxRHqHHVMWe18Zj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "idempotency_key": "ci-fastjson-cve-2026-31337-597dec07c7"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SiPxJVNgEF6n3mUq77jYs2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0134NKVJdTYeenhCemTajrGg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "base": "main", "title": "Upgrade fastjson to 3.1.0 to fix CVE-2026-31337", "body": "Upgrades fastjson from 2.8.0 to 3.1.0 to address CVE-2026-31337 (high severity: unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays). Affected: <2.9.4, >=3.0.0 <3.1.0; fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0.\n\n3.1.0 was chosen over 2.9.4 because the fastjson 3.x migration was completed last sprint.\n\nChanges:\n- requirements.txt: fastjson==2.8.0 -> fastjson==3.1.0\n- CHANGELOG.md: security entry\n\nCI: passed (run ci-0001, sha 597dec07c7).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fastjson-cve-2026-31337"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson to 3.1.0 to fix CVE-2026-31337. CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with a review request to alex: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Version choice:** The advisory says the flaw is fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0. I first tried 2.9.4, the smallest jump from 2.8.0, but the approver turned down that commit. They said the team finished moving to fastjson 3.x last sprint and asked for 3.1.0, so I used that.\n- **Changes:** On the new branch `fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337`, I changed `fastjson==2.8.0` to `fastjson==3.1.0` in `requirements.txt` and added a security entry to `CHANGELOG.md`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `597dec07c7`.\n\n**Worth checking in review:** Before my change, main still pinned fastjson 2.8.0, so this PR is what actually moves the service from 2.x to 3.x. CI passed, but the only test file in the repo is `tests/test_money.py`, so the tests may not fully exercise the 3.x upgrade.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged; a code owner needs to approve it first.", "type": "text"}]}]}